# Reply language

- Default: reply in clear English, even if the user writes in another language (Persian, mixed, etc.).
- Exception: when the user explicitly asks to speak, reply, or explain in a specific language, use that language for the reply.
- Examples of explicit requests: "به فارسی توضیح بده", "speak in Persian", "réponds en français".
- Code, identifiers, and file paths stay as-is in every language.
- After an explicit language request, keep using that language for the rest of the conversation unless the user switches back (e.g. "back to English") or starts a new topic without that request — then return to English default.
